// Scratch contract for `@tao/time`; it graduates to `packages/stdlib/@tao/time/Time.tao` with its
// sidecar `Time.ts` at absorption.
//
// `use time from @tao/time` binds the package under its lowercase service name, so `time.Interval`
// is a call into it (Decisions §9; §11's `use auth from @tao/auth` is the same shape). A lowercase
// name in a `use` line imports the package itself; capitalized names import declarations.

// An interval is a reactive library value: `Value` is the time as of the latest tick, `Running`
// whether it ticks, and `Start()` and `Stop()` control it. It starts when its owning view mounts
// and stops when that view unmounts; `Start()` on a running interval and `Stop()` on a stopped one
// do nothing.
public
type Interval is item {
   Value time
   Running boolean
   Start action()
   Stop action()
}

// `Interval(Every)` constructs an interval that ticks every `Every`. The lowering is the obvious
// one — `setInterval` plus a state update per tick — reached through the expression-position `from`
// (§15), which is the whole bridge: no clock grammar enters the language.
public
function Interval(Every duration) returns Interval {
   return Interval(Every) from ./Time.ts
}
